  "facts": [
    "The original Jordan Bridge, a 1928 vertical‑lift drawbridge, was built for $1.25 million by Carl and Wallace Jordan, whose lumber business demanded a reliable crossing over the Southern Branch Elizabeth River.",
    "In 2004, an oil tanker collision forced the bridge’s east tower and lift span into the river, injuring two employees and shutting the crossing for months, a rare event in its 80‑year history.",
    "The 2012 replacement, costing $142 million, eliminated lift mechanisms and weight limits, introduced all‑electronic tolls, and added a free pedestrian walkway, restoring a vital artery for Hampton Roads traffic."
  ],
